    "https://www.csm.edu/academics/career-pathways/business/": {
      "title": "Find Your Path in Business",
      "description": "Business - College of Saint Mary Skip to content Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected Find Your Path in Business Business isn’t one career, it’s dozens. From strategy to finance to leadership, the skills you build here open doors across nearly every industry. Explore the paths below and find the one that fits where you want to go. Home ◆ Academics ◆ Career Pathways ◆ Business Follow your Interests CSM offers several programs that prepare students for careers in business, management, and organizational leadership across a variety of industries. Marketing, Sales & Brand Strategy + Marketing & sales professionals help organizations connect with audiences, grow brands, and communicate effectively. Students learn how to analyze markets, build campaigns, and use digital tools to reach customers and drive growth. marketing digital marketing sales management business administration project management Finance, Accounting & Business Analytics + Financial professionals help organizations make informed decisions about money, investments, and operations. Students develop skills in financial analysis, budgeting, accounting, and data-driven decision-making. Accounting Business analytics finance financial Planning Data Science Management & Organizational Leadership + Strong organizations depend on effective leaders. This pathway prepares students to lead teams, manage projects, and guide organizations through change while building strong workplace cultures. Business administration Master of science in Organizational Leadership Doctor of Education in Educational Leadership Healthcare Administration & Systems Leadership + Healthcare and logistics organizations require leaders who understand operations, systems, and people. Students learn how to manage complex organizations, coordinate resources, support teams, and improve how services and goods are delivered. Healthcare Administration Supply Chain Management Master of Science in Organizational Leadership Nonprofit, Mission & Community Leadership + Mission-driven organizations need leaders who can manage resources, build partnerships, and strengthen communities. Students learn how to lead nonprofits and organizations focused on service and social impact. Business Administration Project Management Master of Science in Organizational Leadership Business Career Outlook “What are you going to do with a business degree?” Fair question. Using the latest BLS data, here’s a detailed breakdown of real salaries and job growth across finance, marketing, HR, analytics, and more, so you can see exactly where this path leads. Read more Why Choose CSM for Business CSM business students gain the knowledge, experience, and leadership skills needed to succeed. Through hands-on learning and a mission-driven approach, graduates are prepared to lead organizations and make a meaningful impact. Leadership Development Leadership is built into the curriculum, helping students strengthen communication, decision-making, and team leadership skills that employers value. Real-World Experience Students apply what they learn through internships, projects, and partnerships that connect classroom learning with real business challenges. Community Partnerships Located in Omaha, CSM connects students with a strong network of businesses, creating opportunities for internships, mentorship, and career-building connections. explore Our Majors Business Fast Facts 15 CONCENTRATIONS One Degree, Many Paths Customize your education to your goals and the evolving business industry. Internships Get Hands-on Experience Make connections and get confidence to transition from college to career. 1:1 Advising Personalized Support Meet regularly with business faculty to stay on track and reach your goals. Get Ready To Join Us Wherever you’re starting from, we’ll help you build a future with confidence. Visit campus Virtual tour Ask Admissions Apply Business isn’t one career, it’s dozens. From strategy to finance to leadership, the skills you build open doors across nearly every industry. Explore the paths below to find the one that fits. 7000 Mercy Road Omaha, Nebraska 68106-2377 (402) 399-2400 (800) 926-5534 Campus Map Our Mission Campus Store Events Media Community Employment Directory Facility Rental Complaint Processes Privacy & Terms of Use Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Snapchat Pinterest Copyright © 2026 College of Saint Mary. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/academics/career-pathways/education/": {
      "title": "Becoming a Teacher",
      "description": "Education - College of Saint Mary Skip to content Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected Becoming a Teacher Some people just know: teaching is who they’re meant to be. It’s a calling. Before you commit years and tuition to a path, it helps to know what to actually expect: the market demand, the pay, and what each grade level really looks like. Home ◆ Academics ◆ Career Pathways ◆ Education What does it take to become a Teacher ? Becoming a licensed teacher generally follows the same path no matter where you go to school. The process typically takes four years for a bachelor’s degree, or as little as one to two years if you already have a bachelor’s degree. Earn a bachelor’s degree in teacher education or a subject area, with required coursework in teaching methods, child development, and classroom management. Complete field experience in real classrooms, building hands-on skills before you’re leading a class of your own. Pass required certification exams , such as the Core Academic Skills for Educators Test and content-area exams. Complete student teaching , a full-time placement where you teach under the guidance of an experienced mentor teacher. Apply for state licensure once you’ve met all requirements. Choosing An Age Group To Teach Every great teacher remembers the age group that first felt like the right fit, some are drawn to the wonder of early learners, others to the depth of a subject they love. Here’s a look at each path. Birth–3 (Early Childhood) + Shape a child’s earliest years, when learning happens fastest. You’ll build the foundational skills, literacy, social-emotional development, and early curiosity, that set children up for lifelong success. K–6 (Elementary) + Teach across every subject and become the steady presence a child remembers for years. Median salary: $61,000. Over 1.4 million positions nationwide. 5–9 (Middle School) + Guide students through one of the most formative stretches of adolescence, specializing in a subject while helping them navigate rapid academic and personal growth. Median salary: $62,970. About 40,500 openings projected each year. 7–12 (Secondary) + Bring depth and passion to a subject you love, and help students prepare for what comes after graduation. Median salary: around $62,000. Over 1 million positions nationwide. K–6 or 7–12 (Special Education) + Advocate for students who need it most, learning inclusive instruction and individualized planning to help every learner succeed. Median salary: $64,270. About 37,800 openings projected each year. Explore Teacher Education Pathways Already have a bachelor’s degree? If you’re changing careers and already hold a bachelor’s degree, the Master of Arts in Teaching offers an accelerated path to certification, without starting over. Want to lead, not just teach? For experienced educators ready to grow into leadership, CSM offers advanced options like the Doctor of Educational Leadership and a Post-Master’s Certificate in Adult Learning . Why Teach? An Honest look at the profession. Thinking about becoming a teacher? Before you commit to a path, see the real salary and job outlook data for every grade level, elementary, secondary, early childhood, and special education, so you can choose with confidence, not just optimism. Read more ON the Blog Get Ready To Join Us Wherever you’re starting from, we’ll help you build a future with confidence. Visit campus Virtual tour Ask Admissions Apply 7000 Mercy Road Omaha, Nebraska 68106-2377 (402) 399-2400 (800) 926-5534 Campus Map Our Mission Campus Store Events Media Community Employment Directory Facility Rental Complaint Processes Privacy & Terms of Use Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Snapchat Pinterest Copyright © 2026 College of Saint Mary. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/academics/career-pathways/human-services/": {
      "title": "Human Services",
      "description": "Human Services - College of Saint Mary Skip to content Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected Human Services Home ◆ Academics ◆ Career Pathways ◆ Human Services Human Services Careers Programs in psychology and human services prepare students to work directly with individuals and communities while building a strong foundation for graduate study or professional roles. Counseling + Students interested in helping individuals navigate life challenges develop counseling, communication, and advocacy skills. Graduates support families, youth, and communities, with many continuing to graduate study. Psychology & Behavioral Science + Psychology students study how people think, feel, and behave while developing research and analytical skills that support careers in counseling, social services, and graduate study. Community & Social Services + Human services professionals often work in community organizations that provide support programs and services to individuals and families in need. Behavioral & Mental Health + Students interested in mental health careers build a strong foundation in psychology and human development that prepares them for graduate study in counseling, therapy, or social work. Advocacy & Community Leadership + Human services careers often involve advocating for individuals and communities. Students learn how to lead programs, support vulnerable populations, and create positive social change. Why Choose CSM for Human Services Human services students learn by doing. Through field experience, close faculty mentorship, and a mission-driven approach, students gain the skills and perspective needed to support individuals and strengthen communities. Real-World Experience Students complete extensive fieldwork with human services organizations, gaining hands-on experience supporting individuals and families. Faculty Mentorship Small classes allow students to build strong relationships with faculty mentors who guide career exploration, research, and graduate school preparation. Purpose-Driven Focus Rooted in the Mercy tradition, programs prepare graduates to advocate for others and serve communities with compassion and integrity. NUmbers that Matter The numbers below highlight the hands-on experiences, faculty mentorship, and learning environment that prepare students for meaningful careers in human services. 350+ Fieldwork Hours Students gain extensive hands-on experience working in human services organizations before graduation. 11:1 Student to Faculty Ratio The psychology program has an 11:1 ratio, allowing students to work closely with faculty mentors on research and career preparation. Is human services right for you? A career in human services may be a great fit if you: Want a career focused on purpose and meaningful impact Care deeply about helping people and improving lives Are interested in psychology, counseling, or social services Want to advocate for individuals and communities Enjoy listening, problem solving, and building relationships Get Ready To Join Us Wherever you’re starting from, we’ll help you build a future with confidence. Visit campus Virtual tour Ask Admissions Apply 7000 Mercy Road Omaha, Nebraska 68106-2377 (402) 399-2400 (800) 926-5534 Campus Map Our Mission Campus Store Events Media Community Employment Directory Facility Rental Complaint Processes Privacy & Terms of Use Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Snapchat Pinterest Copyright © 2026 College of Saint Mary. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/academics/career-pathways/science/": {
      "title": "Sciences",
      "description": "Sciences - College of Saint Mary Skip to content Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected Sciences Home ◆ Academics ◆ Career Pathways ◆ Sciences Degrees that lead to Science careers CSM offers several science programs that prepare students for careers in healthcare, research, and emerging scientific fields while building the foundation for graduate or professional school. Biology & Life Sciences + Biology programs help students understand living systems, human health, and the natural world. Students gain laboratory experience and build the scientific foundation needed for careers in healthcare, research, and biotechnology. Integrative Biology Molecular Biology Pre-Health Environmental Biology Laboratory Science & Research + Students interested in discovery, experimentation, and laboratory work develop strong research and analytical skills used in scientific and medical laboratories. Chemistry Medical Laboratory Science Forensic Science + Forensic science applies biology and chemistry to help solve crimes and support the justice system. Students learn laboratory techniques, evidence analysis, and scientific investigation used in forensic laboratories and criminal investigations. Forensic Science Chemistry Medical Laboratory Science Environmental Sciences + Science careers also focus on protecting natural resources and studying ecosystems. Students learn how scientific research supports environmental conservation and sustainability. Environmental Biology Sustainability minor Science Education + Students who are passionate about science and teaching can inspire the next generation of scientists by bringing biology and chemistry into the classroom. Secondary Education Why ChoosE CSM For Science Women in science thrive in a supportive environment that encourages curiosity, discovery, and leadership. Through hands-on learning and close faculty mentorship, students build the knowledge and confidence needed for scientific careers and graduate study. Women in Science CSM provides an environment where women are encouraged to pursue scientific discovery, leadership, and innovation in fields where their voices are needed. Hands-On Lab Experience Students gain real laboratory and research experience working alongside faculty, building the technical skills needed for scientific careers and graduate study. Faculty Mentorship Small class sizes allow students to work closely with faculty mentors who support their academic goals, research interests, and preparation for graduate programs. Numbers That Matter The numbers below highlight the hands-on learning, mentorship, and opportunities that prepare students for successful science careers. 10+ Science Pathways CSM offers more than 10 programs that prepare students for careers in science, healthcare, and research. 100% Employment Rate Graduates of the several science programs are employed or pursuing advanced education within 6 months of graduation. 20+ Marie Curie Scholars Application-based program supporting women in science through mentorship and research opportunities. Is Science right for you? A science career may be a great fit if you: Are interested in graduate study or healthcare professions Are curious about how the world works Enjoy research, experiments, and solving complex problems Want to improve health or advance scientific knowledge Like working with data, technology, and laboratory tools Get Ready To Join Us Wherever you’re starting from, we’ll help you build a future with confidence. Visit campus Virtual tour Ask Admissions Apply 7000 Mercy Road Omaha, Nebraska 68106-2377 (402) 399-2400 (800) 926-5534 Campus Map Our Mission Campus Store Events Media Community Employment Directory Facility Rental Complaint Processes Privacy & Terms of Use Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Snapchat Pinterest Copyright © 2026 College of Saint Mary. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/academics/career-pathways/law-legal-services/": {
      "title": "Law & Legal Services",
      "description": "Law & Legal Services - College of Saint Mary Skip to content Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search MyCSM Apply Visit Give Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Career Pathways Mercy Core Curriculum Honors Program Outcomes & Pass Rates Internships Study Abroad Library Registrar Admissions Admissions Overview Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Admitted Students Parent Resources Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Undergraduate Tuition & Fees Graduate Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships FAFSA 101 Student Accounts Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview New Student Experience Student Success Housing Dining Center Clubs and Orgs Faith and Service Campus Inclusion Health & Wellbeing Campus Safety About About Overview Mission History Sisters of Mercy Our Catholic Identity Women’s College Office of the President College Leadership Awards & Recognition Campus Map News Alumni Alumni Overview Homecoming Journeys Magazine Alumni Perks Stay Connected Law & Legal Services Home ◆ Academics ◆ Career Pathways ◆ Law & Legal Services Degrees That Lead to Legal Careers Legal careers require strong analytical thinking, communication skills, and knowledge of the legal system. CSM offers several pathways that prepare students for law school, legal services, and policy roles. Lawyer + Students interested in becoming attorneys develop strong research, writing, and critical thinking skills that form the foundation for law school and legal careers. Coursework emphasizes legal analysis, argumentation, and the ability to evaluate complex issues from multiple perspectives. Professional Legal Studies (pre-Law) Professional Legal Studies (3+3 Creighton Law) Paralegal & Legal Support + Paralegals play a key role in preparing legal documents, conducting research, and assisting attorneys with trial preparation and case management. Graduates may work in law firms, corporations, and government agencies supporting legal teams and preparing cases. Legal STudies Post-Bacc Paralegal Certificate Compliance & Corporate Law + Legal knowledge is essential in business environments where organizations must follow regulations and manage contracts.Career paths may include roles such as contract analyst, compliance manager, or policy specialist. Legal Studies Professional Legal StuDies (Pre-law) Legal Studies (3+3 Creighton Law) Government & Public Policy + Legal training also prepares students for careers in government, advocacy, and public policy where professionals work to shape laws and public programs. Legal Studies Professional Legal Studies (Pre-Law) Professional Legal Studies (3+3 Creighton Law) Why Choose CSM for Law Legal studies students gain practical insight into the legal profession through expert instruction, real-world experience, and accelerated pathways that prepare them for law school and careers in legal services. Learn from Practicing Attorneys Every course in the Legal Studies program is taught by licensed attorneys who bring real courtroom and legal experience into the classroom. Accelerated Law School Pathway Students can pursue the 3+3 law program with Creighton, completing both a bachelor’s degree and Juris Doctor in six years. Real-World Legal Experience Internships and real-world training help students build legal research, writing, and case preparation skills before graduation. LEGAL Studies By The Numbers These numbers highlight the accelerated pathways, professional preparation, and career outcomes that help students launch successful careers in law and legal services. 6 Years to Earn Your JD Earn both a bachelor’s degree and a law degree through the accelerated 3+3 pathway with Creighton Law School. 1 4-year Paralegal Program CSM is the only 4-year paralegal program approved by the American Bar Association in Nebraska and Iowa. 100% Job Placement Rate Historically, 100% of our paralegal certificate graduates were employed in the field within six months of graduating. Is Law Right for You? A legal career may be a great fit if you: Want a career that influences policy and protects rights Enjoy research, writing, and critical thinking Care about justice, advocacy, and public policy Want to analyze complex problems and build strong arguments Are interested in leadership roles in law, government, or business Get Ready To Join Us Wherever you’re starting from, we’ll help you build a future with confidence. Visit campus Virtual tour Ask Admissions Apply 7000 Mercy Road Omaha, Nebraska 68106-2377 (402) 399-2400 (800) 926-5534 Campus Map Our Mission Campus Store Events Media Community Employment Directory Facility Rental Complaint Processes Privacy & Terms of Use Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Snapchat Pinterest Copyright © 2026 College of Saint Mary. All rights reserved."
    }
  },
